      ],
      "source": "https://www.parisdigest.com/paris/champs-elysees-facts.htm",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "King Louis XIV commissioned the avenue in 1667, envisioning it as a grand perspective from the Louvre.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.parisdigest.com/paris/champs-elysees-facts.htm",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Élysée Palace, near the avenue, became the official presidential residence in 1848 under the Second Republic.",
